Shoulder joint labral tear — AAOS (@med-source-labrum: 0, is #reference, #part-of @medicine-sources) { r_66H3KEN7TXRY1BTNEX5F68DASF
American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons, OrthoInfo; article written or reviewed by an ASES member. Shoulder Joint Labral Tear. English. The URL retains the earlier wording Shoulder Joint Tear, Glenoid Labrum Tear.

[Authorized source](https://www.orthoinfo.org/diseases--conditions/shoulder-joint-tear-glenoid-labrum-tear/).

After normal anatomy, read Anatomy of the Shoulder and Types of Labral Tears. For a specific damage question, read Symptoms of a Labral Tear and Diagnosing a Labral Tear, including Medical History and Physical Examination and Imaging Tests. The explanation distinguishes superior, anteroinferior, and posterior labral findings. Symptoms overlap with other conditions.

Read the treatment and recovery discussion only with its particular clinical context; it does not establish the cause of an individual's pain or a universal postoperative schedule. Compare imaging interpretation with the asymptomatic-labrum study and current professional criteria.

